1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
QueueKind: a little help, a human decision.
A silent demonstration using invented requests.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
48 synthetic examples. Six requests to review.
No requests are routed automatically.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Check held-out examples before trusting suggestions.
These small synthetic results do not establish reliability.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Inspect actual mismatches, not just an accuracy number.
Expected labels can also be wrong.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:01:00,000
No suitable route? Hold the request for follow-up.
Held requests are excluded from training.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Read the request and choose a route yourself.
Model scores are not calibrated probabilities.

7
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Export only reviewed decisions, including held requests.
The downloaded CSV is checked against the visible choices.

8
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Apply the routed review, keeping held-out examples separate.
This is the same check set, not new independent validation.

9
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Word-count suggestions have limits. Every request needs review.
No sending, urgency scoring or service-eligibility decisions.
